                    insight_balanced:       `Trust by design: you protected the Brand Trust Index above its 70 floor AND hit the ≥55% containment target, with perceived exploitation low. You shrank the audience inference at its source instead of masking it — a truthful AI efficiency story.`,
                    insight_covert:         `Covert efficiency: you hit the containment savings, but the Brand Trust Index fell below the floor. The privacy-concerned segment is moving deposits and the journalist now has the story — the ₺56M you saved is dwarfed by the trust premium you spent.`,
                    insight_overcorrect:    `Over-corrected: trust is safe, but you delivered only a fraction of the ₺310M the Board was promised. Protecting trust by gutting the AI is not the answer — you still owe the COO a credible containment plan.`,
                    insight_eroded:         `Trust eroded and savings short: the launch hurt the Index without delivering the efficiency story. The classic worst case — design re-built around the audience/exploitation mechanism, not against it.`,
                    insight_kvkk:           `You launched with a confidentiality promise your data-use config contradicts. Under KVKK (Law No. 6698) that is a misrepresentation and a consent failure — a future enforcement action sitting inside an otherwise plausible launch.`,
                    insight_covertflag:     `Your design hid the AI from customers. Covert disclosure (or a fake human persona) is the single fastest way to convert a trust problem into a reputation crisis once the journalist's story runs.`,
                    insight_exploit:        `Perceived exploitation is high — customers feel their data reaches a vast audience. This is the exact driver the research identifies, and it is what pulls the privacy-concerned, deposit-heavy segment away fastest.`,
                    insight_segmentgap:     `Your blended Trust Index looks acceptable, but the privacy-concerned segment — 56% of deposits — sits below the floor. Averaging a calm majority with an angry, deposit-heavy minority hides the risk to the balance sheet.`,
                    insight_savingsshort:   `Annual savings came in below the ₺310M the Board was promised. Reconcile the gap honestly rather than overstating containment — the earnings-call story has to be defensible.`,
                    insight_premium:        `You held the trust premium: the Index, the privacy segment and a low exploitation score all stayed healthy while containment hit target. Trust compounds slowly and depletes fast — you protected the stock.`,

                    hint_kvkk:              `You promised confidentiality your data-use contradicts — a KVKK exposure. Either make the promise real (data minimisation, no training on transcripts) or stop making it.`,
                    hint_covert:            `Your launch hides the AI from customers. Switch to clear disclosure before the journalist's story converts a covert bot into a reputation crisis.`,
                    hint_exploit:           `Perceived exploitation is climbing. Add a kept confidentiality assurance and minimise the data you ingest — those two levers shrink the audience inference directly.`,
                    hint_trust:             `The Brand Trust Index is below the 70 floor. Revisit disclosure, the confidentiality promise and the fallback rule — the privacy segment is dragging the blended number down.`,
                    hint_contain:           `Containment is well short of the 55% savings target. A segmented fallback can still contain routine queries — you don't need to route fraud and hardship to the bot to hit the number.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — trust above the floor, containment on target and exploitation low. Lock it in with full monitoring and a transparent line for the journalist.`,

